- **Collaboration with the University of Renewable Energy**: We have collaborated with the University of Renewable Energy to establish a research program aimed at exploring advanced renewable energy technologies. This program includes student internships, joint research projects, and the development of new technologies. One promising project is the pilot testing of floating solar panel systems that could be deployed on water bodies to minimize land use while maximizing solar energy capture. The insights gained from this partnership will inform our future solar initiatives.

- **Engagement with Local Governments**: GreenGrid Utilities has formed alliances with various local government bodies to promote sustainability initiatives within communities. These partnerships focus on implementing community solar programs that allow residents without suitable rooftop access to participate in solar energy generation. Through these programs, customers can subscribe to a portion of a local solar farm and receive credits on their energy bills, making renewable energy accessible to a broader audience.

